# Documented exceptions for the CI image scan (.github/workflows/image_scan.yml).
# Every entry needs a rationale and a `Revisit:` trigger — enforced by
# spec/code_smells/template_invariants_spec.rb.

# json 2.18.0 ships INSIDE Ruby 4.0.4 as a default gem; Gemfile.lock pins the
# fixed json (>= 2.19.2) and Bundler activates it at runtime, so the vulnerable
# copy is dormant. Unfixable until a Ruby patch release replaces the default gem.
# Revisit: on the next Ruby 4.0.x patch (bump .tool-versions), or 2026-09-01.
CVE-2026-33210

# net-imap 0.6.2 ships with Ruby 4.0.4 (bundled gem); Gemfile.lock pins the
# fixed net-imap (>= 0.6.4) and Bundler activates it at runtime. The app sends
# mail via SMTP and never opens IMAP connections. Same Ruby-patch dependency.
# Revisit: on the next Ruby 4.0.x patch (bump .tool-versions), or 2026-09-01.
CVE-2026-42257
CVE-2026-42258
CVE-2026-42245
CVE-2026-42246

# Go stdlib v1.26.5 baked into thruster 0.1.25's precompiled binary
# (verified: `strings exe/x86_64-linux/thrust | grep go1.` → go1.26.5).
# Eight HIGH findings, mostly DoS-class (asn1/xml/url/http2/tls recursion or
# resource exhaustion) plus x/net idna punycode handling and html/template
# XSS — thruster is the production HTTP front, so partially reachable, but
# 0.1.25 is the newest release and the fix needs thruster to rebuild with
# Go >= 1.26.6. No action available to us. (The 0.1.22-era os.Root entry
# CVE-2026-39822 that previously lived here was cleared by the 0.1.23+
# rebuild — its Revisit trigger — and removed.)
# Revisit: on the next thruster release (> 0.1.25), or 2026-09-15.
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-46600
CVE-2026-56853
CVE-2026-56858
CVE-2026-56859
CVE-2026-56860
CVE-2026-56862
